+Since the sets have the same finite cardinality $p^3$, the map $(u',j)\mapsto u'h_jK_{s+1}$ is a bijection and $\mathrm{tr}\,U'_p f=U'_p\,\mathrm{tr}f$.
+
+\smallskip\noindent\emph{(d).} Let $V$ be trivial, $U^{(p)}=U_1(M)$, so $U_{(s)}=U_s=\Uone{Mp^s}$, $p\nmid M$. By Prop.~\ref{prop:s01-adjoint}(a) (trivial coefficients; the operator $[UhU]$ on trivial $V$ is defined for every $h\in\Bhat^\times$, the action of $h_p$ being absent)
