+
+(C1) \emph{If $g_ih_j=h_jg_i$ for all $i,j$ (e.g.\ $g$, $h$ have disjoint supports and reps are chosen at their supports; or $g$ is central), then $T_gT_h=T_hT_g$.} Indeed
+$T_gT_hf(x)=\sum_{i,j}g_{i,p}h_{j,p}f(xg_ih_j)$ and $T_hT_gf(x)=\sum_{j,i}h_{j,p}g_{i,p}f(xh_jg_i)$ are termwise equal ($g_i,h_j$ commute, so do their $p$-components).
+For disjoint supports $S,S'$ one may choose reps supported on $S,S'$ because $UgU/U=\prod_{v\in S}U_vg_vU_v/U_v$.
+
+(C2) \emph{If $h$ normalises $U$ ($hU=Uh$) and $hg=gh$, then $T_hT_g=T_gT_h$.} Indeed $T_hT_gf(x)=\sum_i(hg_i)_pf(xhg_i)$, where $hg_iU$ runs through the cosets of $hUgU=UhgU$, and
